      "id": "S04-T02-QUALITY-001",
      "severity": "high",
      "summary": "Slack directory tests and codegen proof are false-green against unregistered product schema tables.",
      "details": "The lane adds sourceChannels and channelSyncStates table sources and proves behavior by constructing slackDirectoryDatabaseSchema/transientConvexSchema in the test. However the committed product generated schema imports and registers neither table, while makeSlackDirectoryImpl finalizes with databaseSchema and the action/mutations read and write sourceChannels/channelSyncStates through the runtime schema. The proof packet says generated output is intentionally not committed and transient codegen passed, but for this task the durable Slack directory tables are product runtime state; leaving their generated schema registration absent makes focused tests green without proving the committed product schema can expose the durable tables required by S04-T02.",
